-- title:
--   Square root laws and finite transport-Gini statistics
-- statement:
--   On the common support $\{1,-1,i,-i,0\}$, define the parent multiplicities $(4,4,4,4,0)$ and child multiplicities $(3,3,3,3,3)$, normalized by degrees $16$ and $15$. Define Euclidean pair cost, independent-pair Gini dispersion, all nonnegative coupling matrices with those marginals, their transportation costs, and the infimum of those costs. Define the radial coupling, the source $(X^4-1)^4$, and its proposed normalized child $X^3(X^4-1)^3$. Root and derivative bridge theorems establish that these are actual empirical root laws.
